%% DM26-0670

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Domain as Domain actor
    participant Handler as ProtocolActor<br/>(the builder's)
    participant Config as ConfigurationActor
    participant Crypto as CryptoActor
    participant Protocol as Http or Git<br/>(its own task)
    participant Far as The far end
    participant Read as operation.read<br/>(a blocking thread)

    Note over Domain,Read: As built, 2026-11-04 (docs/architecture/protocol-handlers.md). The domain names an operation it declared<br/>at load (PolarAgent::OPERATIONS). It has no client, no credential, and no way to ask for one.

    Domain->>Handler: ask(operation)
    activate Handler
    opt Location::Configured
        Handler->>Config: the variable, as it is in force
        Config-->>Handler: its value, or nothing (Denied, NotConfigured)
    end
    opt Credential::ForHost
        Handler->>Crypto: UseCredential(pass, BoundTo host)
        Crypto-->>Handler: the name bound to the host, never a value
    end
    Handler->>Handler: judge(operation, declared, target, ...)<br/>and record the verdict, hosts only (polar::protocol)

    alt denied, or the host asked for time, or the credential is held
        Handler-->>Domain: Err(Failure), and nothing is sent
    else allowed
        opt the operation uses a credential
            Handler->>Crypto: UseCredential(pass, Http or Git, name, host)
            Note over Crypto,Protocol: The binding is checked here, where the secret lives.<br/>Any other pass is refused and learns nothing.
            alt not bound to the host, or not registered
                Crypto-->>Handler: refused
                Handler-->>Domain: Err(NotBound or NoCredential), and nothing is sent
            else
                Crypto-->>Handler: the credential, wiped when dropped
            end
        end
        Handler->>Protocol: perform(request, credential)
        deactivate Handler
        activate Protocol
        Protocol->>Far: the request, through the egress proxy and CA
        loop each redirect or auth host (HTTP: git stays on its host, or fails)
            Far-->>Protocol: go there
            Protocol->>Handler: hop(target)
            Handler->>Handler: judged and recorded again
            alt off the credential's binding
                Handler-->>Protocol: Err(Failure): not followed
            else
                Handler-->>Protocol: the credential for there, if any
            end
        end
        alt the credential is refused
            Far-->>Protocol: 401 or 403, or a second challenge (git)
            Protocol-->>Handler: Err(CredentialRefused)
            Handler->>Handler: not presented again until a new version,<br/>and the agent holds Credentials
            Handler-->>Domain: Err(CredentialRefused)
        else it answers
            Far-->>Protocol: the reply, whole and bounded
            Protocol->>Read: read(reply): what came back, never what was sent
            activate Read
            Read-->>Protocol: a value, within its budget
            deactivate Read
            Protocol-->>Domain: Ok(value), as an ordinary message or ask's answer
        end
        deactivate Protocol
    end
